# Example agent-channels.conf for Mission Control Direct Push
# Copy this file to agent-channels.conf and fill in your Discord user IDs
#
# Format: AGENT_NAME|DISCORD_USER_ID|DESCRIPTION
#
# To get a Discord user ID:
#   1. Enable Developer Mode in Discord (User Settings > Advanced > Developer Mode)
#   2. Right-click on a user > Copy User ID
#
# Note: User IDs are numeric and look like: 123456789012345678

# Example entries (replace with your actual agents):
# alice|123456789012345678|Team Lead
# bob|987654321098765432|Developer
# charlie|555555555555555555|Designer

# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file: cp agent-channels.conf.example agent-channels.conf
# 2. Edit agent-channels.conf with your actual Discord user IDs
# 3. Set MC_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN environment variable with your bot token
# 4. Enable push with MC_PUSH_ENABLED=true or use --push flag
